WEBVTT

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.830
Kageki Shojo!!

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.500
Right, let's begin.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.380
Of the beauty I've seen,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:29.510
none caught my eye, save for
the glimmering jewel that is hers!

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.340
In the blink of an eye,
he made the auditorium his own

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.720
and drew in the audience's attention.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.180
<i>This </i>is what a professional
actor is capable of...

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:43.810
Now I am held, imprisoned in her shine,
and my eyes will be caught by no other.

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.680
He's going all-out.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.480
Not even going easy on them.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.810
He's so dreamy!

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.530
His enunciation is so smooth.
You can hear every word so clearly.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.450
He's not speaking that loud,
but his voice just commands attention!

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.450
I'm so glad I didn't have to go with him!

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:59.040
His pace and rhythm emphasize
the most important parts of the line.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.580
His voice is so hot.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:04.880
Andou's not even going to try to
stoop to his students' level.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.960
Can't say I'm surprised. He's not known
for being terribly <i>nice</i>.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:16.260
With what words should I profess
my deepest love for you?

00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.520
Indeed, let me swear this love to you
upon the pale moon above!

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.900
Juliet!

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.650
O Romeo!

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:36.450
Romeo! Wherefore art thou Romeo?

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.660
She's so loud...

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:42.830
Andou-<i>sensei</i>'s performance
tricked her into speaking louder.

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:45.790
He's completely stumbled them.

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.500
Deny thy father and refuse thy name;

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.750
They're really unlucky to go with him.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.130
I feel so bad for them.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.930
Or, if thou wilt not, be but sworn
my love, and I'll no longer be a Capulet.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.930
I don't. Adapting to bad luck
is a skill on its own.

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:56.890
Come on. It's not over for them yet.

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.760
We won't know how they did
until we see who got the roles.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.220
How's Sarasa?

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.400
She just squeezed her eyes shut!

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.110
Sensei!

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:17.160
Tomoe-<i>sensei</i>!

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.240
What is it, Sarasa-<i>san</i>?

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:24.290
Guess what? Dai-<i>sensei </i>promised to
come play <i>kabuki </i>with me today!

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:26.080
Kouzaburou did?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.670
Can I wait for him
in that room over there?

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:32.510
Go right ahead, but mind
your manners, all right?

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:34.090
I will!

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.180
Ten 
minutes 
later

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:46.440
Dai-<i>sensei</i>'s so <i>late</i>!

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.230
Whomst calls me brother? Surely, you jest!

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.650
Dost thou not know who I am?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:55.110
I am the--

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:58.820
I am the very embodiment
of chivalry, the great Sukeroku!

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.330
What folly is this!

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:06.080
What man would dare
declare himself my brother!

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:13.380
This man, O brother!

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:15.760
What a powerful voice!

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.760
But it's not <i>all </i>about being loud.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.270
An actor's old saying says "voice first,
face second, everything else third."

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:27.060
You've got to work on your delivery first.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.480
How do I do that?

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.020
Try speaking from your stomach.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:36.610
Pull air into your tummy,
open your throat, and speak.

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:38.450
Brother!

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:40.950
She just wants to play pretend!

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.950
We may be "playing pretend" on stage,

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.960
but acting is no child's play!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.250
We should always treat it
like the craft it is.

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.460
Isn't that right, Kouzaburou?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:57.760
It's no wonder they call you a "living
treasure." Might I get some lessons, too?

00:03:57.760 --> 00:03:58.840
I swear...

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.470
Crawl through my legs!

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:09.640
What a pitiful samurai!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.730
Indeed!

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.570
Acting is no child's play.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.990
How could I deny my sweet Juliet?

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.580
Ask anything of your nurse, dear girl!

00:04:26.580 --> 00:04:27.660
Here it comes.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:32.040
Sarasa Watanabe's...

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.460
Tybalt!

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:43.850
What blood? My blood?

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:47.560
Tybalt sees the blood on his hands
and realizes he's been stabbed.

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:53.150
The actress raises her hands to show
the audience her expression of despair.

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.190
Focusing their attention.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.150
Romeo, you foul knave!
What hast thou done to me?!

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.360
So in <i>her </i>version,
Romeo is on stage right.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:09.250
No, this can't be! I yet live,
my end cannot be so nigh!

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:13.500
You know why we have <i>mie</i>, Sarasa-<i>san</i>?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.250
It's to focus the audience on the most
beautiful parts of our performance.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:23.220
"Look at me! Look right here!
Look how cool I am!"

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.430
It's how we draw their attention!

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:41.110
Fair Juliet, bright star in darkest sky...

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.780
...I die, hand never knowing
your soft glow.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.580
Her tragic expression softens
as she thinks of her beloved.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:55.500
Wow, she's looking up at the audience
in the balcony seats.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:06:01.590
Shock, hatred, love,
sadness, and finally...

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:06.260
The emotion Watanabe's Tybalt
feels in his final moments:

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:13.640
"Nay, nay, 'tis not I."

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:24.490
...'tis not I. Nor her, my lady.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.310
Oh, wow! That's Akiya, right?

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.440
Isn't he so good, Sarasa?

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.200
I did it better.

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:34.960
Sarasa-<i>chan</i>,

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:40.210
no matter what might stand
in my way, I promise you,

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.420
I <i>will </i>be Sukeroku one day.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:55.020
My life ends by the hand of Romeo.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:02.400
I thought we'd see more of a split,
but I guess not.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.280
Perhaps it's a good thing that the
students can tell who's at what level.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.410
It's easier for them to judge ability by
comparing performances instead of grades.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.120
I hope this will get them even more
fired up about their studies!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:18.880
All that's left is figuring out
who will play Tybalt.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.960
{=0}Tybalt: Sawa Sugimoto, Sarasa Watanabe

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:26.050
The Renaissance period was also when
we saw advents in set and theater design.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.180
It's been three days since auditions.
When will we find out who got cast?

00:07:29.180 --> 00:07:31.220
Why are they making us wait?

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:34.100
I can barely focus on our lecture!

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:36.890
That's all for today's class.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.400
That's all for today's class.

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:38.390
{=1}I'm <i>definitely </i>getting Romeo!
I'm gonna be Romeo!

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.150
All rise!

00:07:40.150 --> 00:07:42.110
Oh, one last thing.

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:47.900
The cast list will be posted on
the first-floor hallway this afternoon.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:51.870
If you've got questions about the results
or your personal performance,

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.540
come to the faculty office.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.370
That's all!

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:56.410
Bow!

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.540
Thank you, sir!

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:01.590
This is weird.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:06.840
I never felt nervous at JPX48 election
or even for the Kouka admission results.

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:12.010
But now I'm feeling more nervous
than I ever have before.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.350
Ai-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.430
Let's go see the cast list together!

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:21.560
Oh, Watanabe-<i>san</i>, what great timing!

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:24.480
You know how Risa was
out sick with a cold today?

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:29.490
So I went down to the room
you cleaned to check it for her,

00:08:29.490 --> 00:08:32.990
but boy, the floor's still filthy, and I
found some cracks in the wood, too.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:37.120
We wouldn't want anyone to step on any
splinters and hurt their feet, would we?

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:39.080
I'd like you to go clean
that room again, right now.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.290
Oh, uh, could you wait just a sec?

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.840
No, right this instant.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.880
Faculty Office

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.210
All right, I'm heading out.

00:08:46.210 --> 00:08:48.670
Are you still sticking around,
Andou-<i>sensei</i>?

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:51.640
Yeah, I'm not done yet today.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.430
Excuse me, sir!

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.720
Sensei! Why didn't I
get picked for Juliet?!

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:00.020
Here comes the first wave.

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:03.100
Good luck.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.730
It's snowing.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.490
Ai.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:14.280
Did you see the cast list?

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.250
Mmkay. Want to go
get something nice to eat?

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:25.130
Ow! Hey! That hurts, Ai.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:29.970
I'm so disappointed.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.880
I know.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.140
The teachers loved your Juliet, Ai.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:42.560
But Shakespeare's Juliet
is an innocent 14-year-old girl

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:46.270
who's obsessed with
the first man she's fallen for.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:50.150
Your Juliet was a bit too mature.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:56.280
I've gotta get even better.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:01.870
I've gotta work much, much, much harder.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.460
Sounds good.

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:07.210
What do you want to eat? <i>Yakiniku</i>?

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.040
I can't go.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.210
Huh?

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:12.550
I'm waiting for Sarasa.

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:16.430
Friends should be there for
one another in times like these.

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:19.810
Huh? What?! No way!

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.770
Huh? What?! No way!

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.850
"Juliet: Ayako Yamada"

00:10:22.770 --> 00:10:25.150
Really?!

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.940
No way...

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.190
Oh, uh...

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:31.440
Oh, uh...

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.230
Romeo: Minami Shirota

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.530
So Aya got Juliet after all.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.290
She's bottom of the class though, right?

00:10:40.290 --> 00:10:42.540
Did she get her parents
to pull some strings?

00:10:43.370 --> 00:10:44.870
Who the hell just said that?

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:48.540
I don't know if you know,
but Aya's family runs a bakery!

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:50.050
If her parents had any say in this,

00:10:50.050 --> 00:10:52.090
that just means you
lost the role to some <i>bread</i>!

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:56.340
And if family meant anything,
then I would've gotten Romeo easy!

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:00.430
Aya got cast as Juliet
because she deserved it!

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.310
Kaoru!

00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:07.520
Thank you, Kaoru!
You don't have to cry for me!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:12.570
I'm not crying for you, I'm crying for <i>me</i>!
I wanted to play Romeo!

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:15.070
But <i>congrats</i>, Aya!

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:21.990
Oh, hey, Watanabe-<i>san</i>,
have you seen the cast list yet?

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.910
What's that look for?

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:27.870
I got to see it! And you know
who got the role?

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:33.590
Just kidding.
I haven't seen it yet, either.

00:11:33.590 --> 00:11:38.720
Boy, you first-years sure are lucky.
You get to do <i>everything </i>early.

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.760
What will you be performing in at
the culture festival, Hijiri-<i>senpai</i>?

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.270
Oh, me?

00:11:44.270 --> 00:11:49.900
I'm playing Scarlett in the <i>Gone With the</i>
<i>Wind </i>segment of our musical number.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:51.360
You're gonna be great!

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:54.610
I suppose. You stopped cleaning.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:59.570
And right after the culture festival,
you have your big debut!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.950
That's right.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.540
I can't wait to get on stage myself.

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:13.340
I'm pooped. My throat's getting sore
from all this talking.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:17.550
Pardon me, sir.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:19.010
There you are.

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:21.640
Might I have a moment of your time?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:27.480
Sarasa sure is late.
Is she still cleaning?

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:30.940
Or did she go home? No, she wouldn't have.

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:42.530
I bet she'll react just like she did
when she got in, all loud and excited.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.620
But this time, I'll get to tell her
I'm so happy for her, too.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.040
But instead,

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:58.130
she quietly stared at the cast list,
focused reverently on her own name.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.120
"Tybalt: Sarasa Watanabe"

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.550
I didn't come out of
disagreement with the casting.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:09.140
I'd just like to know
what it was I lacked.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:13.650
What you lacked, huh? Oh, boy.

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:17.570
Well, you don't have experience yet,
so you're lacking all sorts of skills.

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:21.570
And it's not just you.
It's everyone in your class.

00:13:22.410 --> 00:13:25.700
Do you know the musical <i>Amadeus</i>, sir?

00:13:25.700 --> 00:13:30.210
Yeah, the Broadway show?
The movie was pretty good, too.

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:34.750
It's all about Mozart and Salieri and
the clash between genius and hard work.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.550
And the suspense created
by the rivalry between them.

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:40.720
I hate that musical.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:48.350
When I saw it as a child, I identified
with Salieri, and it scared me.

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:51.230
I can't help but feel that no matter
the skill I possess or praise I earn,

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:57.020
I'll never hold a candle to unprecedented
prodigies like Watanabe-<i>san</i>.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:01.610
That no matter how hard I work,
I'll never outmatch her.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.780
And part of me admires her
for her ability,

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:10.660
but I know that if she hadn't been here,
I wouldn't feel so defeated.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:16.920
That if she hadn't tried out for Tybalt,
it could have been me.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:21.300
I can't help but think these things,
and I hate myself for it.

00:14:21.300 --> 00:14:26.510
But now I'm just ranting, aren't I?

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.390
Please forgive me for
the interruption! Thank you, sir!

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:33.890
You're fine, don't worry. This is better
than you sitting here and sobbing.

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:36.270
Did people really sit here and cry?

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:37.690
More than you'd think.

00:14:37.690 --> 00:14:41.190
If I cried, would that change anything?

00:14:41.190 --> 00:14:43.530
It might make you feel better.

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:46.410
But I'd prefer if you didn't.
I'm not good with tears.

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:48.370
I won't cry.

00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:49.780
Thought not.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:55.670
The first thing you need to know is
most talented people are like Salieri.

00:14:55.670 --> 00:15:01.210
Acting is all about teamwork,
and the Kouka troupe values individuality,

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:04.720
so we don't want a group of all Mozarts.

00:15:04.720 --> 00:15:09.140
If everyone in the troupe were
"unprecedented prodigies,"

00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.720
then it'd feel too bland.

00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:17.440
You should also know that the votes were
evenly matched between you and Watanabe.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:22.230
"Watanabe: 17"
"Sugimoto: 17"

00:15:17.440 --> 00:15:22.320
The teachers took another vote
and we were <i>still </i>split on you two.

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:28.320
Ohgi-<i>sensei </i>came late, so when she
arrived, we had her cast the tie-breaker.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:32.160
Very well, I see where you're
coming from. In that case...

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.670
...Tybalt should be played
by Sarasa Watanabe.

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:40.500
You missed it by a paper-thin margin.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:45.880
So sure, you might've missed out
this time, but don't dwell on it too much.

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:51.350
You're right. You're absolutely right.

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:53.310
Thank you so much, sir.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:16:00.810
Who knew that a single sheet of paper
could cut so deep?

00:16:03.900 --> 00:16:06.280
You'll need to rehearse
on your own time, mmkay?

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.110
Yes, sir!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:11.830
Oh, and I'll come watch you rehearse
three times before dress rehearsal.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.700
Only three times?

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:19.960
The stars of the Culture Festival are the
second-years. You guys are a fun bonus.

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:23.550
Plus, your lines are mostly soliloquys,
with no real interaction between you.

00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:26.800
As long as you can say your lines
without flubbing them, you're good.

00:16:28.300 --> 00:16:30.220
Okay, break a leg!

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:33.850
Well, <i>now </i>this doesn't seem
like that big of a deal.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:36.850
Japanese Room

00:16:33.850 --> 00:16:37.270
There are two months left
until the Culture Festival.

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:41.020
Us second-years will be shifting from

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:44.570
classes to rehearsals for the Festival.

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:50.320
As such, we'll be counting on your class
to help us out for the next two months.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:54.580
The best thing you can do
is try not to trip us up.

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:58.460
<i>Especially </i>since you guys
get to have a little skit in <i>our show</i>!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.670
You'll be playing Romeo, Shirota-<i>san</i>?

00:17:00.670 --> 00:17:04.130
Yes, ma'am! I'll do everything I can
to avoid tripping you up!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.960
And you're playing Tybalt, Watanabe-<i>san</i>.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.760
Are you gonna be okay?

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:13.510
Risa-<i>senpai</i>! You're so nice
to worry for me!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:18.850
We're <i>all </i>worried about you, especially
after you fell at the Sports Festival.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:23.060
And you don't really fit
the image of the dark Tybalt.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:26.230
Watanabe-<i>san</i>'s Tybalt...

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.070
...was incredible.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:34.740
Oh, jeez. This has really
struck a nerve with me, huh...

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.250
Morning.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:43.670
Good morning, Takei-<i>senpai</i>.

00:17:44.630 --> 00:17:49.710
Oh, this? A fan stopped me on
my way here and handed these to me.

00:17:47.420 --> 00:17:51.170
To Tomomi Takei

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:51.260
You're just that incredible.

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:55.390
Nah, I just happen to be
the class representative.

00:17:55.390 --> 00:17:58.270
And I was at the Sports Festival, too.

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:01.390
I'm sorry you didn't get the role.

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:05.110
Being the perfect student
is so boring, huh?

00:18:05.110 --> 00:18:11.990
Everyone expects you to be perfect, and if
you mess up, they won't let you forget it.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:18.610
"Kouka School of Musical
and Theatrical Arts"

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:15.700
And when you're the class rep,
everyone's got their eye on you,

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:18.540
so you always have to be
on your best behavior.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:23.330
You can't help but feel jealous of
prodigies or strong personalities.

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:26.460
Do you feel that way too
sometimes, Takei-<i>senpai</i>?

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:28.340
Oh, all the time.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:32.590
I mean, look at my assistant rep,
she's got way more character than I do.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:37.470
But she says the things that I can't,
which is a huge help.

00:18:37.470 --> 00:18:39.560
To fans of the troupe,

00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:46.810
we'll <i>always </i>be our class representatives.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:49.940
It's a lot of pressure,

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:56.360
"Kouka School of Musical
and Theatrical Arts"

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:56.410
but the skill you've worked so hard
to cultivate will never fail you.

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:57.990
Sure, it's nerve-wracking,

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:02.160
but I'll finally be able to stand on
the stage I've dreamed of this whole time,

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:03.910
and that's enough to get me excited.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:07.250
That's what these two years
have all been about, after all.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:11.960
I'm sure you'll feel
the same way in a year's time.

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:16.090
I'm glad you're the class rep
for the first-years.

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.970
You've kept your class organized,

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:22.180
and that made things easier on me. Thanks.

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:26.230
Huh? Oh, jeez!

00:19:26.230 --> 00:19:30.020
Don't cry now! Save it for graduation!

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:33.610
Why?! I hate crying
in front of other people!

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:34.900
Ugh, I'm so embarrassed...

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:38.490
I feel you. It's so humiliating, huh?

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:41.280
We're pretty similar.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.450
See you later.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.130
Okay!

00:19:56.130 --> 00:20:00.100
You want to know why I chose
Watanabe-<i>san </i>for Tybalt?

00:20:00.100 --> 00:20:01.010
Yes, ma'am.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:06.850
Forgive me for asking so bluntly, but I
was hoping to learn something from it.

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:10.020
I see. Very well, then.

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:15.110
Here's the reason I chose
Watanabe-<i>san </i>over you:

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:20.820
because her Tybalt's Audience
Appeal Level was just a bit higher!

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:25.370
It was difficult to discern
which of the two would rate higher,

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:28.620
but consider this: 80% of Kouka's
audience are women,

00:20:28.620 --> 00:20:33.380
and those women will insert themselves
into the role of Juliet as they watch.

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:38.170
So we must consider what
our audiences want of Tybalt.

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:42.760
"He loves Juliet (me) so much,
he's gone full evil..."

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:42.930
Your Tybalt, shattered by his own love,
was wonderful indeed,

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:52.390
"He only shows his true feelings
to Juliet (me)..."

00:20:42.930 --> 00:20:48.020
but Watanabe-<i>san</i>'s Tybalt, who opened up
about his feelings at the very end,

00:20:48.020 --> 00:20:52.940
would resonate more strongly
with our audience.

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:55.900
I suppose to put it more concisely,

00:20:55.900 --> 00:21:01.030
Watanabe's Tybalt had
<i>much </i>more fangirl potential!

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:02.450
<i>Fangirl!</i>

00:21:04.330 --> 00:21:08.370
Fangirl... That's it! Fangirling!

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:11.500
That one word has made
everything come together!

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:17.670
Ohgi-<i>sensei </i>is truly a diehard Kouka fan!

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:24.220
Whoa, Sawa, you're just coming in?
Usually you're here first.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:25.640
I had some things to attend to.

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:28.560
Sarasa, I've been remiss.

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:29.680
Huh?

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:33.690
Congratulations on getting Tybalt.

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:35.690
Sugimoto-<i>san</i>...

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:45.030
Today, we'll be attending a photo shoot

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:48.830
for the poster advertising school
admissions for next year's class.

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:52.790
Please assemble in
the auditorium this afternoon.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.580
Wait, does that mean...

00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:57.000
We're gonna be on the poster?

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.710
Yes, it's our first real job
for the troupe.

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:03.800
And next year, we'll all be
second-year students.

00:22:07.600 --> 00:22:11.270
Ai-<i>chan</i>, let's keep givin' it
our all every day, together!

00:22:11.270 --> 00:22:16.730
Yeah. And one day, you and I are
going to stand on that silver bridge!

00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:17.820
Yeah!

00:23:44.950 --> 00:23:46.910
The Kouka School of Musical
and Theatrical Arts

00:23:46.910 --> 00:23:49.320
is now accepting applications
for our 101st class!

00:23:49.320 --> 00:23:52.660
Join us on the stage of your dreams!
